graphify-out/

# aime_100 lm-eval task yaml: GENERATED per host, because dataset_kwargs.data_files
# must be an ABSOLUTE path (HF datasets resolves relative paths against CWD and
# lm-eval does not chdir to the task dir). Committing one host's copy guarantees a
# stale pointer on every other host. The DATA (aime_100.jsonl) and the build report
# ARE committed and are byte-identical across hosts.
# Materialise with: python eval/build_aime100_dataset.py --yaml-only
eval/lm_eval_tasks/aime100_chat/aime100_chat.yaml

# RL / replay PROMPT POOLS. Policy: everything publishable IS committed; exactly
# one file is withheld, and only because it is not ours to redistribute.
#
#   scripts/build_lcb_rl_pool.py       -> eval/lcb/lcb_rl_pool.jsonl        COMMITTED
#   scripts/build_gepo_replay_pool.py  -> eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.jsonl WITHHELD
#   scripts/build_replay_manifest.py   -> .MANIFEST.json + .mbpp.jsonl       COMMITTED
#
# LCB is public and ungated (problems come from public contests), so the LCB RL
# pool is committed in full.
#
# The GEPO replay pool is NOT, and this is the whole of the reason: this repo is
# PUBLIC, and that file embeds 250 GPQA questions together with their correct
# answers in plaintext. GPQA is a GATED dataset that ships a canary string
# precisely so its questions do not end up in web crawls and leak into future
# pretraining sets. Publishing them would contaminate GPQA for everyone, not just
# for us, and it is not ours to redistribute.
#
# The pool is still RECORDED here rather than merely asserted, because a training
# basis nobody can inspect is a basis nobody can check:
#   * eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.mbpp.jsonl     — the MBPP tier IN FULL (471
#     rows, CC-BY-4.0, already public).
#   * eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.MANIFEST.json  — the GPQA tier by IDENTITY only
#     (Record ID + gold letter + question sha256, no question or answer text),
#     plus the full pool's sha256 and per-tier counts.
# Anyone with legitimate GPQA access rebuilds the full pool byte-for-byte from the
# committed deterministic builder and checks it against that sha256.
#
# The REBALANCED MIXED POOL (run4 onward) is one file carrying all four tiers, so the
# same rule applies to it, with one difference: its LCB tier is publishable too, so the
# open file holds 599 rows (128 lcb_exec + 471 mbpp_exec) rather than mbpp alone.
#   scripts/build_gepo_mixed_pool.py   -> eval/replay/gepo_mixed_pool.jsonl   WITHHELD
#   scripts/build_replay_manifest.py   -> .MANIFEST.json + .open.jsonl        COMMITTED
# Reproduce:
#   python scripts/build_gepo_mixed_pool.py --lcb 128 --gpqa-nothink 250 \
#       --mbpp-nothink 371 --mbpp-think 100 -G 8 --hours-budget 45
#   python scripts/build_replay_manifest.py --pool eval/replay/gepo_mixed_pool.jsonl \
#       --builder scripts/build_gepo_mixed_pool.py
# then check the result against pool_sha256 in the committed manifest.
eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.jsonl
eval/replay/gepo_mixed_pool.jsonl
